<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Two test assemblies boot the real application through WebApplicationFactory<Program>:
  tests/WebMVC.Tests and tests/WebAPI.Tests. Program reads process-wide configuration, so when
  `dotnet test` runs the four assemblies in parallel, those two hosts can observe each other's
  settings. The symptom is rare and misleading: DemoCertificateDisplayTests occasionally renders a
  target band it should not, roughly one full-solution run in eight, while passing 8/8 when the
  assembly runs alone.

  Serialising the ten app-host classes inside WebMVC.Tests (AppHostCollection) was not enough,
  because the contention is between assemblies, not within one.

  MaxCpuCount=1 makes the runner use one worker per assembly run, which removes the overlap. It
  costs a few seconds and buys a suite that either passes or fails for a real reason.
-->
<RunSettings>
  <RunConfiguration>
    <MaxCpuCount>1</MaxCpuCount>
  </RunConfiguration>
</RunSettings>
